- [Orthopaedic Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/orthopaedic-dog-beds): An orthopaedic dog bed has one job: to carry your dog's weight evenly so their hips, elbows and shoulders never press through to a hard floor. That takes dense, supportive foam that keeps its shape, not fibre that flattens. Every size is listed in centimetres, with a 100-night trial. How to choose an orthopaedic dog bed What makes a dog bed genuinely orthopaedic The word isn't regulated, so plenty of beds use it loosely. Run three checks. The base should be solid foam rather than loose fill. It should be deep enough that your dog doesn't sink to the floor. And it should recover its shape after they get up. Try the fist test: press your fist into the centre. If you can feel the floor, so can your dog. The Nocturne, on profiled egg-crate foam, is a good place to start. Who an orthopaedic bed is for Large and giant breeds, older dogs, dogs who are stiff after exercise, and any dog who has abandoned their bed for the floor because it has gone flat. If your vet has advised firmer support, start here and ask them which shape suits your dog. To browse by size, see large dog beds and extra large dog beds, or by life stage, dog beds for older dogs. Is an orthopedic dog bed the same as an orthopaedic one?Yes. Orthopedic is the American spelling and orthopaedic is the British one. It's the same idea: a supportive foam bed that keeps your dog off the floor. Will an orthopaedic bed help my dog's arthritis?A bed can't treat arthritis, and your vet should lead on that. What a supportive bed can do is stop a stiff dog sinking through to a hard surface, and a low, easy entry means lying down and getting up take less effort. Prefer a softer, moulding feel? Compare memory foam dog beds, or browse all dog beds.
