- [Large Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/large-dog-beds): Big dogs are hard on beds. A fibre-filled bed that looks generous online can flatten under a Labrador within weeks. These large dog beds are listed in real centimetres, from memory foam and orthopaedic styles to raised mesh beds, so what arrives is the size you measured for. How to choose a large dog bed How to size a large dog bed Measure your dog lying stretched out, nose to the base of the tail, and add 15 to 20cm. Labradors, Golden Retrievers and German Shepherds usually land in our Large or XL sizes, depending on how they sleep: curlers can go smaller, sprawlers need the longer bed. The Nocturne, for example, comes in Large (91 × 69cm) and Extra Large (107 × 76cm). Over that? Go to XL and extra large dog beds. Under it? See medium dog beds. Large dogs need foam, not fill The heavier the dog, the more weight goes through the hips and elbows when they lie down. That's why large dogs are best on foam rather than fibre. For the most support, start with orthopaedic dog beds. For dogs who lean, see bolster dog beds. What size bed does a Labrador need?Usually a Large or XL. Measure yours to be sure: nose to the base of the tail lying down, plus 15 to 20cm, then check it against each bed's dimensions. Large or extra large?If your measurement comes out bigger than the largest size here, or your dog is a giant breed, see extra large dog beds. Or browse all dog beds.
- [XL & Extra Large Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/extra-large-dog-beds): If your dog's legs hang off every bed you've bought, you've been shopping in the wrong size range. These XL and XXL dog beds are sized for giant breeds and big sprawlers, with every dimension in centimetres so you can measure your dog, not guess. How to choose an extra large dog bed Why giant breeds need more than a bigger cushion A Great Dane or Newfoundland puts serious weight through their elbows and hips every time they lie down, and a thin or fibre-filled bed collapses under that. Look for deep foam and enough length to stretch out fully. The Mardale XXL is 132 × 104 × 20cm, with memory foam over an egg-crate support base. XL or XXL? Choose XL for big sprawlers and the larger retrievers and shepherds: the Melbreak is 122 × 89cm. Choose XXL for giant breeds such as Great Danes, Newfoundlands, Mastiffs and Leonbergers. Smaller than that? See large dog beds. What size bed does a Great Dane need?Most adult Great Danes need an XXL. Measure nose to the base of the tail while they lie stretched out, add 15 to 20cm, and check that against each bed's dimensions. Can I get an orthopaedic bed in XXL?Yes. Look for orthopaedic and memory foam styles in this collection, or browse orthopaedic dog beds by size. For senior giants, see dog beds for older dogs, or go back to all dog beds.
- [Small Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/small-dog-beds): Small dogs feel the cold faster and love to feel tucked in, but they still need something decent underneath. These small dog beds range from deep, soft nests to memory foam bolsters, in sizes for little dogs, every one listed in centimetres. How to choose a small dog bed Small dogs still need support Long-backed breeds like Dachshunds are better on a flat, even base that keeps the back level instead of letting it sag into the middle. Cushioning on top, support underneath. For firmer options, see memory foam dog beds. Nest or bolster? Curl-up sleepers like Cavaliers and Frenchies often choose a deep nest, such as the velvet Harewood (Small, 46 × 36cm) or the sherpa Windermere (Small, 50 × 40cm). Dogs who stretch out on their side suit a small bolster bed. How big should a small dog's bed be?Big enough to stretch out in: nose to the base of the tail lying down, plus 10 to 15cm. Any bigger and a small dog loses the tucked-in feeling. What bed suits a Cockapoo?Most adult Cockapoos suit a small or medium bed, depending on their size. Measure first, then choose by sleeping style. If yours measures up bigger, see medium dog beds. See nest and donut dog beds, luxury dog beds, or all dog beds. For the most support, compare orthopaedic dog beds.
- [Dog Beds for Older Dogs](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/dog-beds-for-older-dogs): They used to leap onto the sofa. Now they think about it first. An older dog needs a bed that meets them where they are: firm enough that they don't sink to the floor, low enough to step into, and supportive enough to get up from without struggling. How to choose a bed for an older dog What changes as your dog gets older Older dogs sleep more, stiffen more and feel the cold more, and sometimes have accidents they can't help. Their bed has to keep up with all of that, quietly. Three things to look for in a senior dog bed Support first: foam that stops them sinking through to the floor, as in our orthopaedic dog beds. An easy way in: a low front or open side, so there's no step to think about. Easy cleaning: a waterproof or washable cover, so an accident never costs them their bed. The Buttermere memory foam mattress has no edge to step over at all. The Borrowdale gives a memory foam base with a chin rest on every side. What is the best bed for a dog with arthritis?Your vet should guide anything to do with arthritis, and a bed can't treat it. What helps day to day is a supportive foam base that stops your dog sinking to the floor, and a low, open entry so lying down and getting up take less effort. When should I switch to a senior dog bed?There's no set age, and larger breeds tend to stiffen earlier than small ones. If your dog hesitates before lying down, circles more than they used to, or is slow to get up, it's time. For flat, easy-entry styles see dog mattresses, or browse all dog beds.
- [Luxury Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/luxury-dog-beds): You chose your sofa carefully. Your dog's bed sits in the same room. These luxury dog beds are designed to belong there, in velvet, corduroy and rich textures, with the build quality underneath that makes a premium bed worth paying for. How to choose a luxury dog bed What you're actually paying for Not a label. A luxury dog bed earns its price in three places: a base that keeps its shape for years, fabric chosen to handle daily life with a dog, and stitching that holds. Spread over five years, a £150 bed works out at about 8p a night. Choosing a style for your home The velvet Harewood suits softer, layered rooms. The corduroy Kendal pairs a tactile finish with memory foam and cushioned bolsters. Structured dog sofa beds suit modern spaces. Match the bed to the room it lives in, not just to the dog. Are luxury dog beds worth it?If they're built properly, yes. A cheap bed replaced every year costs more over time than one that lasts, and your dog sleeps on a flat bed in between. Our memory foam beds carry a 5-year foam guarantee. Compare memory foam dog beds. Is there a trial on luxury beds?Yes. Every bed comes with a 100-night trial. For the most support, see orthopaedic dog beds, or browse all dog beds.
- [Washable Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/washable-dog-beds): A dog bed collects everything your dog brings home: mud, coat oils, the smell of the park. Washable dog beds let you unzip the cover and wash it, so the bed smells like home again and you're not replacing a whole bed because the cover got grubby. How to choose a washable dog bed Washable or waterproof? Washable handles hair, grime and smells. Waterproof dog beds protect the inside from wet coats and accidents. For puppies and older dogs, look for both, and see dog beds for older dogs. How to wash a dog bed cover Always follow the care label. As a rule: close the zip, wash cool, skip fabric softener (it can trap odours), and let the cover air dry fully before putting it back on. Popular washable styles include the four-sided Ullswater and the fleece-lined Rydal. Can I put the whole bed in the washing machine?Not the foam. Foam inserts shouldn't go in a machine. Remove the cover, wash that, and spot-clean the foam if needed. How often should I wash my dog's bed?Every one to two weeks for most dogs, and more often for heavy shedders or dogs with allergies. Browse bolster dog beds, or all dog beds. For the most support, compare orthopaedic dog beds.
- [Dog Beds Under £100](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/dog-beds-under-100): A good dog bed doesn't have to cost the most, but it does have to be built properly. These dog beds all come in sizes under £100, with the same centimetre sizing, 100-night trial and free UK delivery over £40 as the rest of the range. How to choose a dog bed under £100 Getting the most from your budget Size matters more than finish. A well-sized bed with a simpler cover beats a fancy bed that's too small. Measure first, then choose the best base you can at that size. Memory foam is within reach: the Buttermere memory foam mattress is £99 at 110 × 85cm. The four-sided Ullswater and the high-sided Rydal both start from £69. For big or older dogs Support matters most when your dog is heavy or stiff. If your budget can stretch, compare with orthopaedic dog beds and dog beds for older dogs before you decide. Why do some beds show prices over £100?Some beds come in several sizes. They appear here because at least one size is under £100, and larger sizes may cost more. Is a cheaper bed fine for a small dog?Often, yes. Small dogs put less weight through a bed, so a well-made style under £100 can give them everything they need. See small dog beds, or browse all dog beds.
- [Outdoor Dog Beds & Kennels](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/outdoor-dog-houses): Some dogs would live in the garden if you let them. An outdoor dog bed or kennel gives them a spot of their own out there: off the wet grass, shaded on bright days, and somewhere to watch everything going on. This collection brings together raised outdoor dog beds, an all-weather waterproof bed, plastic dog kennels and canopy day beds. How to choose an outdoor dog bed or kennel Outdoor dog bed, kennel or day bed? A raised outdoor dog bed, like the mesh Bassenthwaite, lifts them off damp ground and rinses clean. The Honister is a foam bed with a PVC-coated cover that wipes clean, for the porch, the garden or the campsite. A plastic dog kennel, like the Blencathra or the ramped Keswick, adds a raised floor and a roof for supervised garden time. A canopy day bed, like the woven Torver, gives a raised, shaded spot to lie on when the sun is out. For more raised styles, see raised dog beds. Placing it well Choose a sheltered spot, out of the prevailing wind, off damp ground and out of all-day sun. Face the doorway away from the weather. Can my dog sleep outside in a dog kennel?Our outdoor kennels and day beds are made for garden time and daytime rest. At night, and in cold or wet weather, your dog's indoor bed is the place. Browse indoor dog beds. Is a dog kennel the same as a dog house?In the UK, "dog kennel" and "dog house" usually mean the same thing: an outdoor shelter. For muddy-paw days indoors, see waterproof dog beds. For their indoor bed, compare orthopaedic dog beds. Do outdoor products have the 100-night trial?The beds do. Outdoor kennels and canopy day beds have a 30-day change-of-mind window instead, with return at your cost. Each product page says which applies.


